# Sentry error reporting — OPTIONAL, and OFF unless this is set.
#
# Read at BUILD time, not at runtime: Vite inlines `import.meta.env.*` as a literal, so with this
# unset the init in src/lib/sentry.ts is dead code and Rollup deletes it. The site still works — it
# just reports nothing to anyone, which is easy to not notice. `npm run build` prints a warning.
#
# For production, set it in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables, then REDEPLOY. Setting it
# after a deploy changes nothing until the next build.
#
# Not a secret: a DSN is meant to be public and Vite inlines it into the client bundle by design.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.sentry.io/<project>

# development | production
NODE_ENV=development
